 ### Inverse Linear Blend Skinning (LBS)
-A method to transform points from world space to unposed space using the inverse of the weighted sum of bone transformations. It is used as the base motion field before residual deformation [S1].
+A method to transform points from world space to unposed space using the inverse of the weighted sum of bone transformations [S1]. It is used as the base motion field before residual deformation [S1].
 
 ### SMPL Model
-A parametric human model used to define the body shape, pose, and part decomposition. It provides the mesh, blend weights, and UV coordinates necessary for the part-based representation [S1].
+A parametric human model used to define the body shape, pose, and part decomposition [S1]. It provides the mesh, blend weights, and UV coordinates necessary for the part-based representation [S1].
 
 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** Training time is significantly reduced compared to prior methods. It is 100 times faster than Neural Body, which typically requires more than 10 hours of training [S1].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** Memory consumption is reduced by adapting the hash table size per part. Uniformly large tables are avoided to prevent excessive memory usage [S1].
-*   **Measured Performance:** On the ZJU-MoCap dataset, the method achieves competitive PSNR. Ablation studies show that the part-based approach (286M params) converges faster and yields higher PSNR than a single MHE-augmented NeRF for the whole body (302M params) [S1].
+*   **Time Complexity:** Training time is significantly reduced compared to prior methods [S1]. It is 100 times faster than Neural Body, which typically requires more than 10 hours of training [S1].
+*   **Memory Complexity:** Memory consumption is reduced by adapting the hash table size per part [S1]. Uniformly large tables are avoided to prevent excessive memory usage [S1].
+*   **Measured Performance:** On the ZJU-MoCap dataset, the method achieves competitive PSNR [S1]. Ablation studies show that the part-based approach (286M params) converges faster and yields higher PSNR than a single MHE-augmented NeRF for the whole body (302M params) [S1].
 *   **Strengths:** Fast training (minutes vs. hours), competitive visual quality, efficient distribution of representational power [S1].
 *   **Limitations:** Requires a parametric human model (SMPL) for part decomposition and motion parameterization [S1].
